  m_Name: 09_Irah_agyamanak_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Irah
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Clack-clack-clack goes the loom! Welcome, traveler!

    When someone
    helps you, gives you something, or does something kind for you, it is important
    to show appreciation.

    In Ilokano, ''agyamanak'' means ''thank you.''

    You
    can use it whenever you want to express gratitude.

    Listen carefully: agyamanak.

    Now,
    try saying ''agyamanak'' yourself.'
